WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.601
-The Republicans are
at each other's throats

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.000
after a small group
of hardliners

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.000
ousted former House Speaker
Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.534
And now, just to add
some more kindling to the fire,

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.033
Donald Trump is
reportedly considering

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:12.801
flying to the Capitol
next week,

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.033
where he might even
pitch himself

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.367
as a candidate for Speaker.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.200
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.133
♪♪

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.300
Donald Trump, the far
and away frontrunner

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.801
for the Republican nomination
for president in 2024,

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.133
has spent most of the week

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.367
in a Manhattan courthouse
on trial for fraud.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.767
In fact, he claimed
he couldn't leave,

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.834
even though he was not
required to be there.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:37.634
-The corrupt attorney
general sued me for fraud,

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.234
and then they found out
they had no case,

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.434
and they have no case.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.968
And today, if you read
the New York Law Journal,

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:48.167
they basically say they have
no case against Trump.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:51.400
But I'm here, stuck here,
and I can't campaign.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.300
I'd rather be right now in Iowa.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.801
I'd rather be in New Hampshire,

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:59.634
in South Carolina or Ohio
or a lot of other places,

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.167
but I'm stuck here.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.267
-He sounds like every single
married couple during lockdown.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:07.567
I'd rather be in Iowa,
New Hampshire,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.767
South Carolina or Ohio
right here.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:11.901
But I'm stuck here.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:12.968
So let me just sit here
and drink

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.200
this entire bottle of merlot

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.701
while I watch "Tiger King"
for the third time.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.567
Again, not even true.
He was not stuck there.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.834
He wasn't even required
to be there.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.501
And yesterday he left
and flew back to Florida.

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:23.234
He chose to show up
so he could say

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.868
ridiculous bull[bleep],
like when he claimed

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.234
the judge in the case
undervalued his

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.834
Florida residence, Mar-a-Lago.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.901
-He's been given
this information.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.267
It's now been proven
to be false,

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.501
such as Mar-a-Lago
in Palm Beach, Florida,

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:38.801
being worth $18 million
when in fact

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.734
it's much closer
to $1.5 billion.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.634
-No one believes your
chintzy Florida swamp hotel

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:49.501
is worth more than the global
box office for "Barbie."

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.567
Your [bleep] Barbie
nightmare house.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.868
This place?

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.734
The hotel that looks like
the [bleep] castle

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.033
you put in a goldfish bowl

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:00.934
so he has something
to look at while he eats?

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.067
This thing looks like
the first house you buy

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.000
when you get drafted
by the Miami Heat.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.234
Remember that photo
from the federal indictment

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.934
on all those boxes of classified
documents in his bathroom?

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.767
That doesn't look like
$1 billion property.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.901
That looks like something
you'd see on "Hoarders."

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:18.167
"Oh, God.
Oh, it stinks in here."

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:21.133
"Well, the toilet doesn't flush,
so I've been using the boxes.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:26.501
Don't open them up.
It's classified."

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:29.000
So the GOP --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.834
So the GOP's frontrunner
for president

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:33.634
is facing four indictments
and a fraud trial,

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.501
probably going to get
kicked off Zillow.

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.067
And on top of that,

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.100
they currently don't even have
a Speaker of the House.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.934
They ousted Kevin McCarthy and
then basically went on vacation.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.667
The interim speaker,
a guy named Patrick McHenry,

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.701
a McCarthy ally,
gaveled the House into recess.

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.701
And as you can see,
he was super pissed about it.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.534
-The chair declares
the house in recess,

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.934
subject to the call
of the chair.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.234
[Slams gavel]

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.801
-You do not expect that energy
from a bow tie guy?

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.300
It's like a dad trying to get
the last piece

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.601
of Ikea furniture to fit.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.434
God damn it!

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:14.400
The clergue
won't fit into the corset!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.934
So they adjourn the House,

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.501
and the reason they did
that apparently was

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.400
that tensions were so high
over the vote to oust McCarthy,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.300
they were genuinely afraid
there would be physical fighting

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.601
if they didn't get the hell
out of there.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.834
-Do you agree with
Congressman McHenry's decision?

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.300
He's the temporary speaker,
The speaker pro temp,

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.033
to put a pause on the week
to let tensions settle?

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.534
-Jake, I'll be really candid.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:38.133
I think if we had
stayed together

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.367
in the meeting last night,

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.234
I think that you would
have seen fists thrown.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.200
And I'm not being dramatic
when I say that.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.000
There is a lot of raw emotions
right now.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.334
I think it was best
to let folks go back home,

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:50.400
decompress a little bit
and then come back together.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.434
-A week? Only a week?

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:55.667
If someone at work did this
in the middle of a meeting,

00:03:55.667 --> 00:04:00.534
I'd say I think we need
to take five...months.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.767
I'll see you guys in March.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.067
Remember, this is the same
GOP caucus that already had

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.868
a near fistfight
on the floor of the House

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:09.067
the first time they had to pick
a Speaker back in January.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.267
You may recall that it took
15 votes last time

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.400
to elect McCarthy with the same
group of hardliners

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.033
holding out
and demanding concessions.

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.868
And as it dragged on,
things got so bad,

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:19.100
members of Congress
were lunging at each other,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.934
including one that had to be
held back by his face.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:24.934
It's one thing to be held back
by your arms or shoulders,

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.834
but your face?

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.534
That's not how you hold back
a congressman.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.801
That's how you grab a cat that's
about to barf on a white rug.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:34.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.601
I really doubt a week is enough
time for everyone to chill out

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:37.901
because they seem really mad.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:39.634
The same guy you just saw there,
Garret Graves,

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.434
was on the House floor
Tuesday yelling about

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.200
the fact that his colleague,
Matt Gaetz,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.234
who instigated the push
to bring down McCarthy,

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:46.868
was fundraising
off the whole thing.

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:48.501
-I keep wondering
what is going on?

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.300
Are we redefining
what conservative is?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.000
What's going on
in this country today?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.701
What's going on in this body?

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:58.133
And all of a sudden my phone
keeps sending text messages.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.267
Text messages saying,
"Hey, give me money."

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.267
Oh, look at that.
Oh, look, "Give me money.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.434
I filed a motion to vacate."

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:11.400
Using official actions,
official actions to raise money.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.901
It's disgusting.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.200
It's what's disgusting
about Washington.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.734
-Even worse,
during his speech,

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.601
he got this text message.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:24.067
And Graves isn't the only one
upset throwing a mini tantrum

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.501
over the GOP mega tantrum.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:26.601
In fact, the GOP infighting

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.067
has gotten so intense
and so personal

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.200
that Republicans are starting
to make salacious allegations

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.801
about each other
on television.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:35.567
For example, here's a GOP
senator named Markwayne Mullin

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.701
talking about Matt Gaetz's
alleged gross behavior on CNN.

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.567
-You got to think
about this guy.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.267
This is a guy
that didn't have --

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:44.434
the media didn't give
a time of day to after

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:47.033
he was accused of sleeping
with an underage girl.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:50.300
And there's a reason why no one
in the conference came

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.934
and defended him because we had
all seen the videos

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:54.634
he was showing
on the House floor

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.167
that all of us had walked away

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.567
of the girls
that he had slept with.

00:05:57.567 --> 00:06:01.434
He bragged about
how he would crush ED medicine

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:04.701
and chase it with
with an energy drink

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.367
so he could go all night.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:07.501
-Not only does Matt Gaetz

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.033
definitely look
like the spokesman

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.133
for an ED-medicine-infused
energy drink,

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:14.767
his name even has a Z
that you know is on the can.

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:16.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:18.400
So he took ED meds and chased it
with an energy drink.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.467
That sounds like something

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:20.868
Rudy Giuliani
would do by accident.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:23.968
"Boss, these Tic-Tacs
don't taste very minty.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:26.567
Uh-oh.

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:28.834
Everyone give me
three inches of space."

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:37.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:38.901
But here's the especially
infuriating thing.

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:41.167
When this small band
of GOP hardliners voted

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.534
to oust McCarthy,
McCarthy could have,

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:45.367
if he really wanted
to keep his job,

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:47.734
reached out to Democrats
to try to win their support.

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:49.701
You know, the same way
he made concessions

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.534
to the hardliners
in his own caucus to get the job

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.100
in the first place.
He didn't do that.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.200
He dissed Democrats.
He told them to "F" off.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.767
So Democrats
voted against McCarthy

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:58.033
for extremely obvious reasons.

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:01.200
And yet Republicans
have the gall to blame Democrats

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.200
for not voting for McCarthy
and bailing them out.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.901
-I think today

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:07.033
was a political decision
by the Democrats.

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:10.634
-Democrats just removed
the Republican Speaker.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:14.367
-Democrats basically
turned on Republicans

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.834
and ousted Kevin McCarthy.

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:20.234
-Every one of the Democrats
voted against McCarthy.

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:21.701
-You had eight,

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:24.200
eight Republicans
that came together

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.133
yesterday with 208 Democrats.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.834
So effectively,
this was a Democrat eviction

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.300
of Speaker McCarthy.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.367
-Are you out of your
[bleep] minds?

00:07:32.367 --> 00:07:33.634
Democrats are in the minority.

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:34.834
You constantly on [bleep] them.

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:36.300
Most of you claim
they stole the election,

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.767
but now you want them
to bail you out

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.934
while you accuse each other
downing Viagra like Pez

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:42.033
and threaten to beat
the [bleep] out of each other?

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.133
Here's a thought exercise.

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:44.434
Let's imagine a world where

00:07:44.434 --> 00:07:46.234
the shoe was on the other foot
and eight Democrats

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:47.767
were threatening
to oust Nancy Pelosi.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:50.701
You think Republicans would come
galloping in to vote for her

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:52.567
and keep her as Speaker
for the good of the country?

00:07:52.567 --> 00:07:55.667
In order to think that,
you'd have to be high on ED meds

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:58.300
and Red Bull and ready
to bang harder than this guy.

00:08:00.767 --> 00:08:03.300
And as if the GOP conference

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:04.868
couldn't become
any more of a cluster [bleep],

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:06.434
some Republicans are floating
the possibility

00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:07.934
of making Trump the Speaker,

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:09.968
since technically it doesn't
have to be a member of Congress.

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:12.100
And when he was asked
about it this week,

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.834
he just didn't dismiss
it out of hand.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.334
-Would you take the job?
Would you take the job?

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:28.667
Would you take the job?

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:42.734
-Yes, tensions are high and
Republicans are near fisticuffs.

00:08:42.734 --> 00:08:44.501
So naturally, the person
to help calm things

00:08:44.501 --> 00:08:46.667
down is Donald Trump.

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:49.767
That's like trying to soothe
a wild stallion with...

00:08:49.767 --> 00:08:50.968
-ED medicine.

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:53.300
0The Republican Party
is such a mess.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.267
They're asking for help from
a guy who's in court for fraud

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:56.834
because no one else
is willing to help them out.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:58.300
The GOP is like a guy
who's so desperate

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.567
for a ride to the airport

00:08:59.567 --> 00:09:00.701
he calls a friend
who's under house arrest.

00:09:00.701 --> 00:09:02.100
-:Yeah, sure,
I can give you a ride,

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.601
but when my ankle bracelet
goes off, you've got to run!"

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:07.567
And now it's being reported
that Trump is planning

00:09:07.567 --> 00:09:09.868
to fly to DC next week
for the Speaker election

00:09:09.868 --> 00:09:11.100
to help figure things out,

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.868
which I am sure
will go smoothly.

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:16.067
-Now to some breaking news.
We just got this.

00:09:16.067 --> 00:09:18.434
Donald Trump may be about
to wade

00:09:18.434 --> 00:09:20.133
right into the middle
of the fight

00:09:20.133 --> 00:09:22.334
over the next Speaker
of the House.

00:09:22.334 --> 00:09:24.601
Let me tell you a little bit
about what we know.

00:09:24.601 --> 00:09:26.501
This is being considered
by Trump.

00:09:26.501 --> 00:09:28.334
He has not been back
to the Capitol

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.501
since before January 6th,

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:33.734
but he's thinking
about coming, apparently,

00:09:33.734 --> 00:09:36.267
maybe he thinks
that he can somehow help

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:38.767
unify the party at this time.

00:09:38.767 --> 00:09:40.934
-Is it really a smart idea
to go back to the Capitol

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:42.601
after what Trump did
on January 6th?

00:09:42.601 --> 00:09:44.734
I mean, I'm no legal expert,
but he's been indicted.

00:09:44.734 --> 00:09:46.234
I'm not sure
you're supposed to go back

00:09:46.234 --> 00:09:47.634
to the scene of the crime.

00:09:47.634 --> 00:09:49.934
He's like a guy who gets
busted on "To Catch a Predator"

00:09:49.934 --> 00:09:52.701
then goes to the same house
a second time.

00:09:52.701 --> 00:09:55.767
"Whoa, Chris Hansen again?!

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:57.167
What are the odds, man?"

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:59.133
"What do you have in the bag?"
"Same thing as last time."

00:09:59.133 --> 00:10:02.200
Mike's hard lemonade
and Twizzlers.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.434
But apparently Trump might not
just be going back to help.

00:10:04.434 --> 00:10:05.868
He might be going to
take the job himself.

00:10:05.868 --> 00:10:07.801
Politico reported today
that Trump is open

00:10:07.801 --> 00:10:09.434
to pitching himself
as a speaker candidate,

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:10.868
according to
a Republican familiar

00:10:10.868 --> 00:10:12.167
with internal discussions.
You know what?

00:10:12.167 --> 00:10:13.467
Good.
Let Trump have a job

00:10:13.467 --> 00:10:15.133
that sucks where half the people
in the room

00:10:15.133 --> 00:10:16.267
hate his guts
and he can't do [bleep].

00:10:16.267 --> 00:10:17.701
He'll be miserable by day two.

00:10:17.701 --> 00:10:20.133
It's all boring procedure
and filing legislation

00:10:20.133 --> 00:10:22.300
and saying mind-numbing
